# Responsive UI (always)

Every screen and component must stay usable and aligned on all devices. Treat this as a hard gate before shipping UI.

## Required viewports

Mentally (and when verifying) check at least the widths in `VIEWPORTS` / `BREAKPOINTS` from `~/lib/constants`:

`320 · 375 · 430 · 768 · 1024 · 1280 · 1440 · 1920`

## Hard rules

1. **Mobile-first** — base styles for the smallest width; enhance with `sm` / `md` / `lg` / `xl` / `2xl`. Never design desktop-only then “shrink”.
2. **No page horizontal overflow** — `documentElement.scrollWidth` must not exceed the viewport. Carousels/marquees stay inside `overflow-x-auto` or `overflow-x-clip` parents; never let fixed/`w-max` tracks widen the page (especially in RTL).
3. **Width fluid, not fixed** — prefer `%` / `min()` / `max-w-*` / `flex-1` / `minmax(0, …)`. Avoid fixed pixel layout widths that force overflow under ~375px.
4. **`min-w-0` on flex/grid children** that shrink or host scrollers. Page shells use `container-page` / `Container` (`max-width: 100%`, `min-width: 0`).
5. **Logical properties only for layout that flips** — `ps`/`pe`, `ms`/`me`, `start`/`end`, `text-start`/`text-end`. No physical `left`/`right`/`ml`/`mr`/`pl`/`pr` for directional layout.
6. **Images** — predictable aspect ratio; `max-w-full` / `sizes` that match breakpoints; no intrinsic width blowing the layout.
7. **Crowded chrome** — on very narrow widths, collapse labels (`sr-only` / icon-only) rather than overflowing the header/nav.
8. **One job per breakpoint change** — stack → row/grid only when space exists; keep touch targets usable (~44px).

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — fixed track widens the page; physical sides; no min-w-0
<div className="flex">
  <div className="flex w-max ml-4">…</div>
</div>

// ✅ GOOD — clipped/scrollable region; logical + min-w-0
<section className="overflow-x-clip">
  <div className="flex min-w-0">
    <div className="min-w-0 flex-1 overflow-x-auto ps-4">…</div>
  </div>
</section>
```

## Checklist before finishing UI work

- [ ] Looks correct at 320 and 768 (not only desktop)
- [ ] No horizontal page scroll in RTL or LTR
- [ ] Header/footer and carousels do not escape the viewport
- [ ] Typography and spacing stay readable; no overlapping controls
